# D-Sign · CueSmith Digital Signage Generator

A modern, high-precision client-side web application for designing and exporting broadcast- and display-grade digital signage graphics, running orders, lower thirds, and notices.

Rebuilt from the ground up implementing the **CueSmith Modernist Design Language** with architectural typography, tabular numerical metrics, strict 0px border radius, 2px structural dividing rules, and an end-to-end direct manipulation **drag-and-drop interaction suite**.

---

## What's New in Version 2.1.0

### 1. First-Class Transparent PNG Image Layers
- **32-Bit Alpha Preservation**: Import, position, and composite transparent cutouts, logos, icons, badges, stamps, and graphics with complete 32-bit truecolor RGBA alpha preservation.
- **Native Resolution & Metadata**: Automatically inspects native pixel dimensions upon upload (`ORIG: W × H PX`) and maintains crisp raster fidelity.
- **In-Place Image Asset Replacement**: Swap out layer graphic assets on the fly with **Replace Image** without losing position coordinates, rotation, scaling, or drop shadows.
- **Photographic Grayscale Treatment**: Modernist high-contrast pure black-and-white treatment toggle (`grayscale(1) contrast(1.08)`) for monochrome signage aesthetics.

### 2. Full Sizing & Proportional Scaling Suite
- **Direct Dimensions**: Fine-grained tabular input fields for Width ($W$) and Height ($H$) in physical canvas pixels.
- **Aspect Ratio Lock**: Proportional lock constraint prevents distortion while scaling or resizing via inputs or corner handles.
- **Continuous Scale Slider**: Tabular numerical slider scaling layers from $10\%$ up to $500\%$ of native dimensions.
- **One-Click Quick Sizing Presets**:
  - `100%`: Instantly reset layer to native pixel dimensions.
  - `Fit Width`: Proportionally scale layer to $80\%$ of total canvas width.
  - `Fit Height`: Proportionally scale layer to $80\%$ of total canvas height.
  - `50%`: Rapid half-scale reduction.

### 3. Direct On-Canvas Manipulation & Magnetic Snapping
- **Interactive Corner Resize Handles**: 4 active corner handles (`nw`, `ne`, `se`, `sw`) with un-rotated matrix un-projection math, enabling natural drag-resizing even on layers rotated at arbitrary angles.
- **Rotation Stalk & Grip**: Dedicated 24px vertical stalk with circular grip positioned above top-center of the active layer for intuitive direct rotation.
- **Magnetic Angle Snapping**: Dynamic snapping to standard angular candidates ($0^\circ, \pm 45^\circ, \pm 90^\circ, \pm 135^\circ, \pm 180^\circ$) within a $\pm 3.0^\circ$ magnetic threshold. Hold <kbd>Shift</kbd> to snap strictly to $45^\circ$ increments at any angle.
- **Rotation Presets**: Dedicated quick-rotation buttons for `0°` (reset), `-90°` (counter-clockwise), `+90°` (clockwise), and `180°` (flip).
- **On-Canvas Coordinate & Rotation HUD**: Live tabular numerical metrics displayed above the active bounding box during translation, resizing, and rotation (`X: 50.0%  Y: 50.0% · W: 400px · ∠ 45.0°`).

### 4. Silhouette Drop Shadow Suite
- **Cutout Silhouette Drop Shadows**: Projects shadows conforming to non-transparent alpha contours of cutouts and icons rather than rectangular bounding boxes.
- **Interactive Controls**: Dedicated controls for shadow color (hex + picker), blur radius ($0\text{–}60\text{px}$), and offset coordinates ($X$ and $Y$).
- **Dual Pipeline Fidelity**: Rendered in the browser preview via high-performance CSS filter dropshadows (`drop-shadow(...)`) and baked into high-resolution PNG exports using native HTML5 2D Canvas shadow pipelines (`ctx.shadowColor`, `ctx.shadowBlur`, `ctx.shadowOffsetX`, `ctx.shadowOffsetY`).

### 5. Unified Stacking & Layer Management
- **Polymorphic Layer Architecture**: Unified text and image layer manager with seamless z-index ordering.
- **Visual Identity**: Miniature $24 \times 24\text{px}$ checkered thumbnails for transparent PNG layers and high-contrast Modernist tags (`PNG` in accent red vs. `TXT` in neutral ink).
- **Drag-and-Drop Reordering**: Drag layer cards up or down with live insertion guidelines to modify visual stacking order.
- **One-Click Reordering**: Step layers up or down with dedicated arrow controls.
- **Layer Duplication & Deletion**: Duplicate any selected layer (<kbd>Cmd / Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>D</kbd>) with automatic $+3\%$ coordinate offset, or delete with <kbd>Delete</kbd> / <kbd>Backspace</kbd> (enforcing a minimum 1 layer safety rule).

### 6. Template ZIP Package Schema Version 2
- **Self-Contained Portable Packaging**: ZIP archives package all graphic cutouts directly under `images/layers/` along with the background image and custom fonts.
- **Lightweight Clean Schema**: `template.json` records relative asset paths (`images/layers/...`) while omitting bloated Base64 data URLs.
- **Automatic Asset Restoration**: ZIP loader unpacks binary PNG blobs, reconstructs clean data URLs, and creates live `HTMLImageElement` instances in the browser cache.
- **Backwards Compatibility**: Schema v2 fully migrates legacy Schema v1 project definitions and text layers, normalizing coordinate representations and property defaults seamlessly.

---

## CueSmith Modernist Design Language

- **Architectural Typography**: Set entirely in **Archivo** (400–900 weight ramp) with tabular numbers (`font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`) across all dimensions, coordinates, angles, and aspect ratios.
- **Color Discipline**: Light ground (`#f3f2f2`), surface (`#eae9e9`), and dark ink (`#201e1d`) with a single live accent red (`#ec3013`).
- **Strict 0px Border Radius**: Zero rounded corners (`--radius-sm: 0px`, `--radius-md: 0px`, `--radius-lg: 0px`) across all cards, buttons, badges, inputs, and preview containers.
- **2px Structural Dividers**: Major functional sections separated by strong 2px rules (`--color-divider`).
- **Flush-Left Label Alignment**: Button labels align flush to the left padding edge per Modernist guidelines.
- **Daylight & Backstage Modes**: Theme toggle switching between standard Daylight office mode and Backstage Dark mode (`#161514` ground) for low-light control rooms.

---

## Screen Formats & Production Export

- **Standard Broadcast & Display Presets**:
  - HD Landscape ($1920 \times 1080$, 16:9)
  - HD Portrait ($1080 \times 1920$, 9:16)
  - 4K Landscape ($3840 \times 2160$, 16:9)
  - 4K Portrait ($2160 \times 3840$, 9:16)
  - Custom pixel dimensions (up to $8000 \times 8000$)
- **High-Resolution Production PNG Export**: Renders exact 1:1 raster canvas graphics with 2D transformation matrices, text line wrapping, letter spacing, drop shadows, backing plates, and alpha blending.
- **JSON Project Portability**: Save and load lightweight JSON signage definitions with embedded data URLs.
- **Template ZIP Packages**: Save and load complete self-contained portable archive packages.

---

## Template ZIP Package Format (`.zip`)

D-Sign exports and loads self-contained **Template ZIP archives** (`D-Sign-Template-[preset]-[timestamp].zip`) using JSZip:

```
D-Sign-Template-[preset]-[timestamp].zip
├── template.json      # Layout schema, coordinates, styling, and relative asset paths (Schema v2)
├── images/            # Background graphic asset (PNG, JPG, WebP)
│   └── layers/        # Binary 32-bit transparent PNG layer cutouts
└── fonts/             # Custom binary font files (.ttf, .otf, .woff2)
```

### `template.json` Schema Version 2 Reference

```json
{
  "app": "digital-signage-generator",
  "framework": "CueSmith-Modernist",
  "dSignVersion": "2.1.0",
  "schemaVersion": 2,
  "preset": "landscape",
  "width": 1920,
  "height": 1080,
  "bgImageName": "stage_backdrop.png",
  "bgImagePath": "images/stage_backdrop.png",
  "bgSizeMode": "cover",
  "bgZoom": 1.0,
  "bgOffsetX": 0,
  "bgOffsetY": 0,
  "bgGrayscale": false,
  "canvasBgColor": "#0b0f19",
  "enableTint": true,
  "tintColor": "#000000",
  "tintOpacity": 40,
  "layers": [
    {
      "id": "layer_1710000000000_abc12",
      "type": "image",
      "name": "channel_logo.png",
      "imagePath": "images/layers/layer_1710000000000_abc12_channel_logo.png",
      "origWidth": 480,
      "origHeight": 240,
      "aspectRatio": 2.0,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 180,
      "scale": 0.75,
      "lockAspectRatio": true,
      "x": 85.0,
      "y": 15.0,
      "rotation": 0.0,
      "opacity": 90,
      "visible": true,
      "grayscale": false,
      "enableShadow": true,
      "shadowColor": "#000000",
      "shadowBlur": 16,
      "shadowX": 4,
      "shadowY": 4
    },
    {
      "id": "layer_1710000000001_def34",
      "type": "text",
      "name": "Main Headline",
      "textContent": "LIVE BROADCAST NOTICE",
      "textFontFamily": "Archivo",
      "textWeight": "800",
      "textAlign": "center",
      "x": 50.0,
      "y": 50.0,
      "rotation": 0.0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "visible": true,
      "textFontSize": 70,
      "textLineHeight": 1.2,
      "textLetterSpacing": 1.5,
      "textColor": "#ffffff",
      "enableShadow": false,
      "enableBgBlock": false
    }
  ],
  "activeLayerId": "layer_1710000000000_abc12",
  "customFonts": []
