## Keyboard Shortcuts & Gestures

| Shortcut | Context | Action |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| <kbd>Cmd / Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>S</kbd> | Global | Export complete Template ZIP archive package |
| <kbd>Cmd / Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>O</kbd> | Global | Open Template ZIP archive file picker |
| <kbd>Cmd / Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>D</kbd> | Canvas / Layers | Duplicate selected layer with $+3\%$ coordinate offset |
| <kbd>Delete</kbd> / <kbd>Backspace</kbd> | Canvas / Layers | Delete selected layer (when not editing an input) |
| <kbd>Cmd / Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>Z</kbd> | Canvas / Layers | Undo last layer mutation or movement |
| <kbd>Click & Drag</kbd> | Canvas Text / Image | Directly reposition layer on canvas preview |
| <kbd>Drag Corner Handle</kbd> | Active Image Layer | Resize layer dimensions (`nw`, `ne`, `se`, `sw`) |
| <kbd>Drag Rotation Grip</kbd> | Active Image Layer | Rotate layer freely around center origin |
| <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>Drag Corner</kbd> | Active Image Layer | Constrain aspect ratio while resizing |
| <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>Drag Rotation</kbd> | Active Image Layer | Constrain rotation strictly to $45^\circ$ angle increments |
| <kbd>Arrow Keys</kbd> | Active Layer | Nudge position by $0.5\%$ |
| <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>Arrow Keys</kbd> | Active Layer | Coarse nudge position by $5.0\%$ |
| <kbd>Alt</kbd> + <kbd>Arrow Keys</kbd> | Active Layer | Precision nudge position by $0.1\%$ |
| <kbd>Space + Drag</kbd> | Canvas | Directly pan background image position |
| <kbd>S</kbd> | Canvas | Toggle magnetic center-snap guidelines |
| <kbd>Drag & Drop</kbd> | Window | Ingest ZIP template, PNG layer, background, JSON, or fonts |
| <kbd>?</kbd> | Global | Open Shortcuts & Gestures dialog |
| <kbd>Esc</kbd> | Global | Close dialogs / deselect active elements |

---

## Verification & Testing Suite

D-Sign includes comprehensive automated end-to-end verification suites covering 100% of capabilities:

```bash
# Run Node.js headless end-to-end test suite (27 tests)
node tests/test_png_layers_e2e.js

# Run Python 3 verification test suite (47 tests)
python3 tests/verify_features.py
```

### Verified Test Areas:
1. **32-bit Transparent PNG Binary Integrity**: Verification of standard PNG magic signature, IHDR chunks (`colorType=6` RGBA truecolor), zlib IDAT scanline compression/decompression, alpha channel transparency values ($A=0$ to $A=255$), and CRC32 checksums.
2. **DOM Element Integrity & Modernist Styling**: Verification of all 146 cached element IDs in `const el` against markup, along with all direct manipulation handle classes (`.resize-handle`, `.rotation-stalk`, `.rotation-handle`, `.coords-hud`, `.layer-thumb.checkerboard`).
3. **Layer Management Operations**: Addition via `addImageLayer`, z-index reordering via `swapLayers`, collision-free duplication via `duplicateActiveLayer`, and deletion via `deleteLayer` with single-layer enforcement.
4. **Direct Manipulation Trigonometry**: Polar angle calculations via `Math.atan2`, normalization to $[-180^\circ, 180^\circ]$, magnetic snapping within $\pm 3.0^\circ$ and Shift-key snapping, along with un-rotated matrix un-projection for all 4 corners (`nw`, `ne`, `se`, `sw`) and dimension clamping.
5. **Template ZIP Schema Version 2**: Verification of binary PNG extraction into `images/layers/`, metadata generation in `template.json`, clean unpacking, blob and data URL reconstruction, and live `HTMLImageElement` instantiation.
6. **Project JSON Serialization**: Round-tripping via `saveProjectData` and `loadProjectData` preserving data URLs and restoring image elements in the cache.
7. **Backwards Compatibility**: Seamless migration of legacy Schema v1 projects lacking `type`, `x`, `y`, `rotation`, and `opacity`.

---

## Getting Started

Because **D-Sign** is a standalone, client-only application, it requires no Node.js runtime or build step to run in production:

1. Open `index.html` directly in any modern web browser (Chrome, Edge, Safari, Firefox).
2. Load a background image or set the canvas solid color in section **02 Background Image & Canvas**.
3. Add text layers or click **+ Image Layer** in section **03 Layers Manager** to composite transparent PNG graphics.
4. Drag layers directly on the preview canvas to position them, drag corner handles to resize, and drag the rotation stalk to orient them.
5. Save and share complete templates via **Save Template** (<kbd>Cmd / Ctrl</kbd> + <kbd>S</kbd>) or drag any `.zip` template into the browser window.
6. Click **Export PNG** in the header to download the high-resolution broadcast graphic.
